        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "54fb0a00-e2b1-5071-ad64-3e7f71c5ce64",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Maremma Sheepdog, Austrian Pinscher\n- Places: Italy, Abruzzo, Maremma, Tuscany, Lazio, Austria\n- Concepts: livestock guardian dogs, farm dogs, shepherding, home guarding, droving\n\nFacts:\n- The Maremma Sheepdog, or Cane da pastore Maremmano-Abruzzese, is a breed of livestock guardian dog indigenous to central Italy, especially Abruzzo and the Maremma region of Tuscany and Lazio.\n- Italian shepherds have used the Maremma Sheepdog for centuries to guard sheep from wolves.\n- The Austrian Pinscher, also called Österreichischer Pinscher and listed as FCI No. 64, is a medium-sized pinscher-type dog breed from Austria.\n- In Austria, dogs of the Austrian Pinscher type were originally farm dogs that kept barns free of rats and served as home guards, livestock guardians, and drovers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
